# How to Translate Shopify Apps

Shopify merchants often use several apps to manage their stores.

The problem is that third-party Shopify apps may use a language that isn't comfortable for every merchant.

If you are looking for a way to **translate Shopify apps**, you can use a browser translation extension such as Page Translate.

## Why Shopify apps can be difficult to translate

Shopify apps are created by different developers.

Because of that, each app may have its own:

- Interface
- Settings
- Buttons
- Forms
- Navigation
- Help text
- Dashboard
- Reports

An app may support English while providing limited or no support for your preferred language.

## How to translate a Shopify app

You can translate a Shopify app directly in Chrome with Page Translate.

### Step 1: Install Page Translate

Install Page Translate from the Chrome Web Store.

**[Install Page Translate](CHROME_WEB_STORE_URL)**

### Step 2: Open Shopify Admin

Log in to your Shopify store and open the app you want to use.

### Step 3: Start Page Translate

Open Page Translate from Chrome and select the language you want to use.

### Step 4: Translate the app

Page Translate translates the visible content of the Shopify app while you continue working.

## Can you translate different Shopify apps?

Yes.

The purpose of a browser-based translator is that it works at the browser level rather than requiring every Shopify app to implement its own translation system.

This makes it useful when you regularly use multiple third-party Shopify apps.

## Translate Shopify app settings

Some Shopify apps contain large settings pages with many labels, descriptions, buttons, and options.

Instead of translating each item manually, you can translate the page while working with the app.

## Translate only what you need

You can also translate selected text when you don't need to translate the whole Shopify app.

For example:

- A setting description
- An error message
- A button
- A product-related term
- A help message

